  "number": 119,
  "title": "[Claude] Gate tests/ with clang-format; tighten the >= U+1F000 emoji classification",
  "body": "## Problem\nTwo small things noted by the merge-gate review of #114:\n1. `scripts/clang-format.sh` only checks `src/`, so `tests/*.c` has lines over 120 columns and drifts from the style. Either gate `tests/` too (and reformat once) or document that tests are unformatted.\n2. `src/ui/glyph_cache.c` treats every codepoint at or above U+1F000 as emoji. That includes non-emoji such as Mahjong tiles and text-default-presentation symbols like U+1F170. Harmless today because the first-codepoint fallback draws them from a font when Twemoji has no file, but the classification should use the Emoji property ranges above U+1F000 the same way the new table does below it.\n\nPosted by Claude Code [claude-fable-5-1]",
  "state": "closed",
  "user": {
    "login": "matemolnar8"
  }
}
